{
    "background_story": "Van Coon was a rugged outdoorsman and trapper who lived in the late 19th century. He made a name for himself in the American wilderness, known for his exceptional skills in tracking and hunting raccoons. Van's expertise earned him the nickname 'Raccoon Van,' and his services were sought after by many a farmer and settler looking to protect their crops from the clever critters. Despite his tough exterior, Van had a soft spot for the raccoons and often found himself at odds with those who sought to harm them. He believed that the coons were intelligent and resourceful creatures, deserving of respect. Van's adventures and exploits became the stuff of local legend, with tales of his raccoon-tracking prowess passed down through generations.",
